# The regional format database: one region per line,
#   name,date,time,number,week,weeknumbers
# each field a word from libc's tables (userland/libc/locale.c). The
# region's display name is its Choice.<name> in settings.d/locale.region.
# Formats follow glibc's locale data (/usr/share/i18n/locales), with
# four-digit years throughout and ASCII where glibc uses U+202F. Where
# glibc's short date is in another script (jp, cn, tw, kr) or names the
# month (ae, eg), the row takes the numeric short date CLDR gives:
# 2026/10/28, 2026. 10. 28., 28/10/2026. The week starts on glibc's
# first_weekday (Sunday when it names none); weeknumbers is on where
# glibc's week rule is ISO 8601's (a week's fourth day decides it).
